<title>FRANCE: Vallourec sees improved 1997 result.</title>
<headline>Vallourec sees improved 1997 result.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>French tube maker Vallourec said after reporting a rise in profit in 1996 on Tuesday that it expects its consolidated results to improve in 1997 despite a rise in raw material prices.  </p>
<p>The company made the forecast in a results statement issued after the stock market closed and which said net attributable profit rose to 196 million francs in 1996 from 85 million francs a year earlier.</p>
<p>&quot;The favourable trend in orders will result in a rise in turnover in 1997 on a like-for-like basis which, linked to a rise in productivity, should lead to a further advance in consolidated results, despite the rise in raw materials prices,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
